      "problem": "What is the remainder when  $-12{x}^{4}+28{x}^{3}-47{x}^{2}+25x-9$ is divided by $6{x}^{2}-5x+4?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2{x}^{2}+3x-4 \\\\  & 6{x}^{2}-5x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-12{x}^{4}+28{x}^{3}-47{x}^{2}+25x-\\phantom{0}9\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-12{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,18{x}^{3}-39{x}^{2}+25x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{18{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+12x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-24{x}^{2}+13x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,24{x}^{2}+20x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-7x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-2{x}^{2}+3x-4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-7x+7.$",
